//   currentConstrainedOut := [], and IsValidPrefix([]) holds by method precondition.
//   EOS break leaves insideConstrainedOut = false, implication vacuous.
//
// Phase 2 OpenConstrainedSpan: Runs only when !insideConstrainedOut. Postcondition
//   sets insideConstrainedOut := true and currentConstrainedOut := [].
//   IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition.
//
// Phase 3a RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure: Postcondition guarantees
//   resultConstrained is always parser-valid. We assign
//   currentConstrainedOut := resultConstrained, re-establishing IsValidPrefix.
//   insideConstrainedOut is unchanged (still true).
//
// Phase 3b rollback then regenerate: We explicitly set currentConstrainedOut := []
//   (IsValidPrefix([]) by precondition) before calling RegenerateUnitOnGroundingFailure
//   again; the postcondition of the second call re-establishes IsValidPrefix.
//
// Phase 4a CloseConstrainedSpan: Sets insideConstrainedOut := false (implication
//   vacuously true) and clears currentConstrainedOut := [].
// Phase 4b CloseSpanWithinBudget: Postcondition directly guarantees
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//
// Invariant 2 (progress): |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
// Phase 1: Each UnconstrainedStep increments steps by 1 and appends at most 1
//   visible token (0 for EOS, 1 for non-EOS). Invariant preserved per iteration.
//
// Phase 2: OpenConstrainedSpan increments steps by 1 and appends exactly 1
//   delimiter token. Net 1:1, invariant preserved.
//
// Phase 3a: We set generated := stablePrefix + r1 where stablePrefix is the
//   portion of generated before currentConstrainedOut. Each visible token in r1
//   costs at most 1 budget step (rejected/rolled-back tokens consume budget
//   without growing visible output), so |r1| <= budget1. Thus
//   |generated| = |stablePrefix| + |r1| <= |stablePrefix| + budget1
//   = (|generatedPrefix| + old_steps) + budget1 = |generatedPrefix| + new_steps.
//
